# CityIRA — Zain Foundation Implementation Plan

**Scope:** Zain's section of `cityira-backend-handoff.md` — Tasks 1–7 + smoke gate.  
**Out of scope:** `app/nodes/`, multi-node graphs (Eagle), full pytest suite (Shaka).  
**Success criteria:** `./backend/scripts/smoke_test.sh` passes with `MOCK_LLM=true`.

---

## Execution Strategy

We use a **contract-first, parallel-wave** model based on the agent briefs.  
You (Zain) run each wave **as a single Antigravity session** — one wave at a time, in order.

```mermaid
flowchart LR
  W0[🏗️ Wave 0 — CONTRACT\n~1 hr] --> A[⚡ Agent A\nLLM / Gemini]
  W0 --> B[⚡ Agent B\nContradiction]
  W0 --> C[⚡ Agent C\nIngest Flow]
  W0 --> D[⚡ Agent D\nPlan Flow]
  W0 --> E[⚡ Agent E\nSimulate Flow]
  W0 --> F[⚡ Agent F\nTrace + Baseline]
  A --> I[🔗 Wave 2\nIntegrator]
  B --> I
  C --> I
  D --> I
  E --> I
  F --> I
```

> [!IMPORTANT]
> Wave 0 must finish and be committed before Wave 1 agents start. It freezes the shared interfaces that all agents depend on.

---

## Wave 0 — CONTRACT (do this first, alone)

**Goal:** Freeze all shared types and stub APIs so Wave 1 agents never block on each other.

### [NEW] `backend/app/llm/__init__.py`
Empty package init — exposes `get_llm_provider` from factory.

### [NEW] `backend/app/llm/schemas.py`
Pydantic models matching `plan.md §4.10.3`:

| Model | Fields |
|-------|--------|
| `ClassificationResult` | `incident_type`, `severity`, `urgency_score`, `confidence`, `reasoning` |
| `ResolvedConflict` | `winning_incident_id`, `resolution`, `confidence`, `low_confidence_resolution`, `rationale` |
| `NotificationDrafts` | `operator`, `public` (≤280 chars), `department` |
| `ContradictionGroup` | `incident_ids`, `distance_m`, `age_diff_minutes`, `conflict_reason` |

Also includes enum helpers to convert `ClassificationResult` ↔ internal `IncidentType`/`Severity` enums.

### [NEW] `backend/app/llm/protocol.py`
```python
class LLMProvider(Protocol):
    def classify(self, incident: Incident) -> ClassificationResult: ...
    def resolve_contradiction(self, incidents: list[Incident]) -> ResolvedConflict: ...
    def draft_notifications(self, incident_id: str, incident_type: str) -> NotificationDrafts: ...
```

### [NEW] `backend/app/llm/prompts.py`
System prompt constants only (no logic). Three prompts from `plan.md §4.10.4`:
- `CLASSIFIER_SYSTEM_PROMPT`
- `RESOLVER_SYSTEM_PROMPT`
- `NOTIFICATION_SYSTEM_PROMPT`

### [NEW] `backend/app/llm/mock_provider.py`
Ports current `_mock_classify`, `_mock_notifications` from `llm_tools.py`. Returns `ClassificationResult` / `NotificationDrafts` Pydantic models (not raw dicts).

### [NEW] `backend/app/llm/factory.py`
```python
def get_llm_provider() -> LLMProvider:
    if settings.mock_llm or not settings.google_api_key:
        return MockLLMProvider()
    return GeminiLLMProvider(...)   # stub — Agent A fills real impl
```

### [MODIFY] `backend/app/tools/contradiction.py` *(stub only)*
Create file with frozen public API that returns empty/minimal stubs:
```python
def detect_contradiction_groups(incidents) -> list[ContradictionGroup]: return []
def score_source(incident, now) -> float: return 0.5
def resolve_group(incidents) -> ResolvedConflict: ...  # minimal valid object
```
Agent B replaces the bodies without renaming anything.

### [MODIFY] `backend/app/tools/llm_tools.py`
Delegate `classify_incident` and `draft_notifications` to `get_llm_provider()`.  
Keep `resolve_contradiction` as-is temporarily (Agent A wires properly).

**Wave 0 done when:**
```bash
cd backend
uv run python -c "from app.llm.schemas import ClassificationResult; from app.tools import llm_tools, contradiction"
# existing run_plan / smoke still pass
```

