## Open Questions

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Q1 — Single session or true parallel?**  
> Do you want me to implement all waves sequentially in **this single Antigravity session** (fastest for a hackathon), or do you want to open **separate IDE sessions** per agent for true parallelism (as described in the plan)?  
> _Recommendation: single session, wave-by-wave — avoids git worktree overhead for a 36-hr sprint._

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Q2 — `GOOGLE_API_KEY` availability**  
> Is your `GOOGLE_API_KEY` already set in `backend/.env`? Agent A needs it to verify real Gemini calls. If not, Mock path will be the only verified path.

> [!NOTE]
> **Q3 — `contradiction.py` file existence**  
> The tools directory currently has `geo.py`, `llm_tools.py`, `resources.py`, `routing.py` — **no `contradiction.py` yet.** Wave 0 will create it fresh. Confirm this is expected.
